<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-sick-wnt-dkk-hair-follicle-code-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Sick et al. (2006) & Andl et al. (2002) WNT/DKK reaction-diffusion hair follicle spacing, secondary wave insertion, transgenic phenotypes & (Pass 3) 3D dermal condensate FGF20/BMP4 chemotaxis with hair peg downgrowth — Code-to-model traceability: 90/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Every modelling block carries an equation/figure citation: the docstring maps the WNT/DKK PDEs, the secondary-wave law and the transgenic regimes to Sick et al. figures and the new Section 3b to Huh 2013 / Glover 2017 / Botchkarev 1999 / Mou 2006 / Paus 1999 / Keller-Segel 1970 (L654-L677); function docstrings restate the equations; the six Lean laws are named in the docstring and registered with updated code loci in the math KG yaml. Deductions: Pass 2 shipped a docstring claiming 22 K14-Wnt placodes while the code produced 32 — fixed now, but it shows the numeric claims in prose are not generated from the run (-4); stage thresholds 0.25/0.5 (L888-L891) and the DC registration radius 2.5 px (L873) are uncited conventions (-3); the FGF20 source normalisation (L806-L807) has no stated biological rationale (-3)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-code-traceability> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/code-traceability" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "2002-sick-wnt-dkk-hair-follicle.py L888–L891: Ordinal stage thresholds at 25%/50% of slab depth are a model convention without a cited morphological criterion <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/64526a0/2002-sick-wnt-dkk-hair-follicle.py#L888-L891>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-sick-wnt-dkk-hair-follicle-code-traceability-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-sick-wnt-dkk-hair-follicle-code-traceability-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-sick-wnt-dkk-hair-follicle-code-traceability-3> ;
    pk:hasScore 9e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-sick-wnt-dkk-hair-follicle-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Sick et al. (2006) & Andl et al. (2002) WNT/DKK reaction-diffusion hair follicle spacing, secondary wave insertion, transgenic phenotypes & (Pass 3) 3D dermal condensate FGF20/BMP4 chemotaxis with hair peg downgrowth — Model fidelity to source: 86/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The WNT/DKK core is still faithful: saturating activator-inhibitor PDEs with the exact unsaturated steady state, Jacobian, d_c = (sqrt2+1)^2 and dispersion (L171-L249), 1D primary -> secondary insertion (L341-L397), 2D regimes (L509-L652). Pass 3 adds the requested dermal dimension as a reduced but mechanistic model: FGF20 sourced by placodes, dermally produced BMP4, Keller-Segel chemotaxis with volume filling in conservative form, peg depth slaved to the DC (L654-L969), with a correct linear analysis showing condensation is epidermally instructed (L726-L768; Lean Law 4). Deductions: the coupling is one-way and the epidermis never deforms (-4); the K14-Wnt regime changes D_w, D_h and kappa together with rho_w (L600-L603) so the 'overexpression' phenotype is not a single-parameter perturbation (-4); BMP4 is produced uniformly in proportion to rho with no interfollicular-epidermal source (L836) and the FGF20 source S(x,y) is a thresholded, rescaled w rather than a modelled Fgf20 transcriptional response (L806-L807) (-3); no parameter is taken from Sick et al.'s SOM table and the dermal constants are hand-tuned (-3)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "2002-sick-wnt-dkk-hair-follicle.py L600–L603: K14-Wnt 'overexpression' preset also changes kappa 0.02 -> 0.015, D_w 0.015 -> 0.008, D_h 0.45 -> 0.32: confounded, not a pure rho_w perturbation <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/64526a0/2002-sick-wnt-dkk-hair-follicle.py#L600-L603>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-sick-wnt-dkk-hair-follicle-model-fidelity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-sick-wnt-dkk-hair-follicle-model-fidelity-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-sick-wnt-dkk-hair-follicle-model-fidelity-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-sick-wnt-dkk-hair-follicle-model-fidelity-4>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-sick-wnt-dkk-hair-follicle-model-fidelity-5> ;
    pk:hasScore 8.6e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-sick-wnt-dkk-hair-follicle-morphometric-validation> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Sick et al. (2006) & Andl et al. (2002) WNT/DKK reaction-diffusion hair follicle spacing, secondary wave insertion, transgenic phenotypes & (Pass 3) 3D dermal condensate FGF20/BMP4 chemotaxis with hair peg downgrowth — Morphometric validation: 84/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "`measure_morphoeval()` (L1457-L1609) now returns 13 measurements with units, methods and sources: d_c, w_*, secondary doubling ratio, WT count vs specimen, K14-Wnt ratio, Dkk1/equal-diffusion count, domain scaling r, and six dermal quantities (DC/placode ratio 1.0 vs Huh 2013; Fgf20-null + chemotaxis-null DC count 0; DC-placode offset 0.41 px vs 0; Fgf20-null/WT peg ratio 0; chi_f sweep r; mass drift 0). Deductions: the only quantitative specimen comparison (NN-spacing CV) disagrees and is reported in a note rather than as its own measurement with a pass/fail band (-5); the K14-Wnt ratio now carries no reference because the Pass 2 '2.0' was unsourced (-3); the Fgf20-null peg ratio 0 and the DC/placode ratio 1.0 are partly by construction (no FGF20 -> no gradient -> no DC) rather than independent validation (-4); WT peg depth 67% of slab has no empirical reference (-4)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/morphometric-validation" ;
