<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-sick-wnt-dkk-hair-follicle-specimen-match> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Sick et al. (2006) & Andl et al. (2002) WNT/DKK reaction-diffusion hair follicle spacing, secondary wave insertion, transgenic phenotypes & (Pass 3) 3D dermal condensate FGF20/BMP4 chemotaxis with hair peg downgrowth — Morphological realism / specimen match: 80/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Panels B1-B3 and C1 are visually distinct and the segmented specimen with its Delaunay graph is shown side by side with the PDE lattice; row D now shows the 3D condensates, an x-z section with pegs and the genotype downgrowth curves, and the GIF carries a 15-frame Phase 3. Deductions: the Pass 2 claim that the WT lattice 'matches the 16 segmented placodes' was a seam-duplication artifact — the corrected count is 15 periodic maxima (14 components) and, more importantly, the nearest-neighbour spacing regularity disagrees (CV 0.086 PDE vs 0.323 specimen) (-8); the specimen is a Gad1 in situ of vibrissa/hair placodes (Maddox & Condie 2004), not Sick et al.'s pelage pattern, so the comparison is a stand-in (-5); row D has no histological or live-imaging reference image (Huh 2013 / Glover 2017 / Paus 1999) beside the model, so DC shape, depth and peg morphology are judged against nothing (-5); the saturated 'ringing' regime (B3) shows plateaus, not the annular rings described in the text (-2)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-specimen-match> ;
